      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To minimize spoilage, immediately increase the reefer unit's setpoint to 4°C or lower, even if it means ventilating a part of the container to prevent overheating. Also, turn off cold room fans to allow the cooled temperature to spread throughout the container. An SOS alert should be sent to the ship's master to divert to the nearest port and offload the shipment as soon as possible. \n\nRegarding safety protocol, if the temperature has been at or above 8°C for at least 2 hours, the batch of premium fatty tuna may be considered compromised. In this situation, further testing (e.g., microbiological checks or organoleptic evaluation) should be done to confirm the batch's quality and safety before it can be sold.",
